From 15459560024a31db4c8cac19ab805715ef4831f0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 06:05:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] fix(front): decline a LET of a temporal formula that
 holds an INSTANCE

The front end binds a LET's definitions as it reads the specification
and the properties, but not the INSTANCEs a LET holds, so a
specification written `LET I == INSTANCE Inner WITH ... IN I!Spec`
read as one without an initial predicate, and the check reported that
the configuration specified none, where TLC checks the model. Such a
LET now declines, in the specification, the properties and the
subscript of [][Next]_v.
